<title>CANADA: Ocelot pipe unit wins TCPL deal.</title>
<headline>Ocelot pipe unit wins TCPL deal.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>O.J. Pipelines, a unit of Ocelot Energy Inc, said on Monday it was awarded a C$40-million contract from TransCanada PipeLines Ltd to build a new pipeline in northwestern Ontario.</p>
<p>O.J. said construction of the line, in the Geraldton and Longlac areas, called for 51 km of 42-inch pipeline and hydrostatic retesting of two valve sections.</p>
<p>The project was slated to start on January 6. The scheduled in-service date was April 1, 1997.</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
